// Twin of score 2 of input/regression/part-combine-silence.ly.
// Same book as pcsil-a-probe: "Rests must begin and end simultaneously to be merged
// into the shared voice" — here the silence is followed by solo and a2.
//
// Pitches: LP's argument-less \relative resolves these to D4 F4 E4 (read off the
// staff-positions -5 / -3 / -4 in the LP grob dump, not guessed from the spelling).
// Lily# `d` = D4, so the twin says d / f / e.
//
// What LP does with it (measured, scratch/lpreg/pcsil-b.log):
//   bar 1: r4 vs r8 -> apart-silence, both printed; then part 2 solo (Solo II);
//          then f vs f -> a2, and it is PART TWO that carries the ink — the solo
//          promoted it, so the shared voice is fed from part 2 and part 1 goes null.
//   bar 2: r8 vs r4 -> apart-silence, both printed; part 1 solo (Solo); e vs e -> a2
//          with part 1 back in the shared voice.
octave absolute
time 4/4

part vone { clef treble }
part vtwo { clef treble }

section A {
  vone { r4 f2. | r8 f e2. | }
  vtwo { r8 d f2. | r4 e2. | }
}

form main { ~A }

score main { combinedStaff { vone vtwo } }
